// Ch10 side errand (optional; requires ch10_drowner_defeated and ch10_reached_reedhollow). A Kirru widow asks for the
// net her mate left in the dead channel. The party brings it; she does not take it. She asks them to lay it at the
// standing places, the way the Kirru give things back. Sets ch10_returned_net. Kirru speech: literal, no idiom.
title: ch10_side_the_three_nets
location: ch10/reedhollow
---
<<if $ch10_returned_net>>
    Kirru as "Kirru widow" [neutral]: It is in the water now. Thank you. #line:ch10_nets_001
<<else>>
    Kirru as "Kirru widow" [neutral]: My mate's net is still in the channel. Where the three went. I cannot go there yet. #line:ch10_nets_002
    -> We'll bring it. #line:ch10_nets_003
        Rhen [neutral]: We'll bring it back to you. #line:ch10_nets_004
        Kirru as "Kirru widow" [sad]: Not to me. Bring it to the standing places, and put it in. He will want it. #line:ch10_nets_005
        Asha [tender]: We will. #line:ch10_nets_006
        <<set $ch10_returned_net = true>>
    -> Not now. #line:ch10_nets_007
        Kirru as "Kirru widow" [neutral]: Then not now. The net will wait. Nets are good at it. #line:ch10_nets_008
<<endif>>
===
